Currently, there seems to be no straightforward way to download and install packages from PyPI or other sources directly from a script. My suggestion is to turn pip into a built-in library, allowing us to use it seamlessly in scripts. This would provide a cleaner, more elegant way to handle package installations without relying on command-line calls.

For example:

import pip

try:

if pip.search_package(package_name):

pip.download_package(package_name, path=".", file_name=package_name)

pip.install_package(package_name)

except Exception as e:

print(e)

This approach would allow us to catch errors in a more controlled manner, as using command-line pip can make error handling more difficult and less graceful.

