except Exception as exc:

results[url] = '%r generated an exception: %s' % (url, exc)

else:

results[url] = len(data)

if not keep_running:

break

requests.post('http://my-server/urls', json=results)

Sometimes an individual URL fails to load in a way that takes an unacceptably-long time to fail, for example a firewall along the way blocks the TCP SYN packet and the underlying OS has TCP parameters that mean it’s many minutes before a timeout is raised. In those cases I’d like a way to break out of the executor and post() the results that have arrived back to my-server .

